Z||000000||BENGAL4||09-24-2001||12:41 AM||||BENGALS 21<BR>RAVENS  10<P>What a game. Bengal defense had 6 takaways. In fact , the defense kicked their ass. Offense had them guessing all day. <BR>Ravens were out played, Brian Billick was out coached and WE BEAT THE WORLD CHAMPS.<P>Bengals 2-0 in September. AWESOME.||||reg||10
Z||000001||Black88GT||09-24-2001||01:09 AM||||LOL I was waiting for some bungles fan to post here.<P>He who has forgotten who has had the worst record in the NFL for the past 10 years.<P>He who has forgotten who won the super bowl last year.<P>The Ravens obviously didn't have their heads in the game (6 turnovers proves that w/o a doubt).  Even their record setting D can't save them when the Offense keeps giving up the ball on their own 30 and 40 yard lines.  BTW, the Bungles D played ok, but allowing 382 total yards is by no means "kickin ass".  <P>Did Corey Dillon break 100 yards?  Yeah I they really kept the ravens Defense guessing lol.  We had more yards per pass BTW.<P>Well guess what.  The Bungles have to play the Ravens at home later on in the season.  You can bet when we romp them I will be back here to post.  <P>I will also be back here to post when the Bungles fail to make the playoffs for the 150th consecutive year.<P>Yes, the Bungles played good enough to pull off the upset, I'll give them that.  But the way the Ravens played I think the Baltimore school of the blind could have whooped em.  I think S. Sharpe said it best "If you can’t get the ball in from the 1, you don’t deserve to win anyway."||||reg||1
Z||000002||BENGAL4||09-24-2001||02:00 AM||||Just take your medicine Jeff. All that losing is in the past. Were talking about this season. It's not what the Ravens did to lose, it's what the Bengals did to WIN. <P>With no running game, the Ravens had to pass. The Bengals pressured Grbac all day. On offense, they kept the Ravens in their nickel package for most of the game. That changed what the Ravens could do on defense. We moved the ball and scored when we needed to. It could have been worse, If Darnay Scott styas in bounds, that a touchdown. Our kicker missed 3 field goals. It could have been 30 - 10. <P>Thats OK, I will have a great Monday, I hope you do too.<P>Bill<BR>86GT<BR>3800 S/C<P><BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||09-24-2001||08:49 AM||||I am having a great Monday, because the Browns won too.  Ty Detmer...7 INT's?  HA HA HA<P>I was at Mid-Ohio all day yesterday...couldn't believe my ears when I turned on the radio and heard BENGALS 21, RAVENS 10.<P>Looks like for the third year in a row, I am going to lose my "Bengals vs. Browns" bet with the mouthy Bengals fan in our company's sales dept.||||reg||10
Z||000004||Cheever3000||09-24-2001||08:57 AM||||Yeah, when I heard the Bengals won I was like  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"> .  But then I remembered all the years they started the season like that and then went down like the Titanic.  This being my last season to cheer for them before the Texans dominate the NFL, I will continue to hope, but won't put any money on them.<P><P>------------------<BR><I>Chuck Hodges</I><BR>Vice President, <A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||4
Z||000005||Black88GT||09-24-2001||12:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever3000:<BR><B>Yeah, when I heard the Bengals won I was like   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif">  .  But then I remembered all the years they started the season like that and then went down like the Titanic.  This being my last season to cheer for them before the Texans dominate the NFL, I will continue to hope, but won't put any money on them.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Cheever said it best.  If any of you Bungles fans care to wager on the next Ravens/Bungles game, I would be more then willing to take that bet.  Anyone? Anyone?<P>Its not what the Bungles did to win, its what the Ravens did to lose.  They had fumbles left and right, punt return fumbles, our pathetic running back fumbled.  Then Grbac with his interceptions.  If you look at 2 of them, he had more then enough time to make a decent pass or even throw it away.  That one interception at the end there was a bit lucky, that guy must have a 52" vertical or something because I have never seen a football player jump that high to get a pass like that.  The Bungles had just over 200 yards total offense.  That tells me right there they didn't do anything to win.  We screwed ourselves.<P>As long as we don't ever get beat by the Skins, I will always have good mondays.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||BENGAL4||09-24-2001||08:04 PM||||You couldn't have been watching the same game I was. All of the Ratbirds turnovers were FORCED errors, made by a swarming defense. The game was actually won in the 3rd quarter. The second half kickoff was not fumbled, it was taken away. the ratbirds first possesion ended when Todd Heep fumbles. Take those forced errors and Grbacs interception to end the 1st half, and that is a 21 point swing.<P>Face it Jeff, I think you will have a few more bad Mondays, because the Ravens offense is terrible. Yes they did throw for 300+ yards, but that's with 64 attempts.<P> With no running game, your defense is going to be on the field alot. And with every game, a title game (teams get up more for the defending champs), the Ravens might suffer the fate of a few defending champions and miss the playoffs all together.<P>Will we win in Baltimore? Who knows. It's hard to win on the road. Will we be competitive? Absolutely. These aren't the bungles any more. They are the BENGALS.<P> As for a wager, I'll bet ya. You figure up what you want to lose, and lets go for it. And remember one thing. The final score was,<P>BENGALS  21<BR>RAVENS   10<P>That's the last word. HA.<P>Bill<BR>86GT<BR>3800 S/C<P>PS. My car can whip your car too.||||reg||10
Z||000007||Black88GT||09-24-2001||08:25 PM||||Forced errors haha.  Like when McAlister caught the ball then dropped it right away, yeah thats a forced error all right.  Our O line played like sh!t but Grbac is used to that.  He made some dumb mistakes but had an overall good game.  As I said before, our yards per pass average was better then the Bungles so it doesn't matter how many attempts we had.  <P>We will see what the Bungles will do this year.  Competitive?  Maybe but if history has taught us anything, they will finish with yet another losing season.<P>Grbacs interception in the first half was a fluke play, admit it.  The ball bounced off practically ever player on the field.  If the ball would have landed in the hands of a Raven it would have been 10-0.  But like I said things like that just didn't swing our way that game.  <P>Ravens offense is terrible?  lol.  We won the SUPER BOWL (remember that thing? prob. not its been so long) with Dilfer as our QB.  Now we have Grbac who is a pro-bowl Qb not to mention upgrading O-line (Searcy is out until Oct. though).  How did that Bungles offense do last year?  Hmm...<P><BR>p.s. I am very close to closing a deal on a 3rd gen RX7, which with $1000 worth of work (mostly maintenance things) will run low 12s.  I don't have the Fiero anymore.  Get your facts straight before you run your mouth.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||87ECO5||09-24-2001||08:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BENGAL4:<BR><B>PS. My car can whip your car too.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Mmmmm ... not sure if I'd play that card yet, Bill!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   LOL!!!||||reg||6
Z||000009||BENGAL4||09-24-2001||09:54 PM||||Did you read the Sun this morning? They said the same thing regarding the forced errors. I guess you know more than the sports writers huh? <P>Competitive? Yea we were competitive enough to kick the Ravens ass back to Baltimore.<P>Grbac's interception a fluke? Well you guys won a few games last year on those types of fluke plays. Remember Ray Lewis's interception right out of Eddie George's hands in the AFC championship game?<P>As for the Ravens offense and winning the Super Bowl, they dont have the same offense they had last year. They won a championship with defense and special teams. I will admit they are the best defense, I have ever seen play and I've seen a few.(70's Steelers, Dolphins & Vikings, 85 Bears). But, last year is history and it is what have you done for me lately.<P>Finally, as for me getting my facts before shooting off my mouth, how was I supposed to know about your car problems? Let me know when mommy and daddy get you a new car and we will talk about a wager or a race.<P>||||reg||10
