Z||000028||BENGAL4||09-27-2001||06:48 AM||||I wont let you make this private.<P>Written by Black88GT<P>I put I changed my mind to explain the reason why I edited it. If I didn't want to wager anything, I would have JUST put I changed my mind. Why would I leave the amount up there if I edited it? <BR>I truly feel sorry for you. You probably get off your dead end job around 4 or so, come home sit on the couch and drink a few beers before dosing off, then doing it all over the next morning. Now that football season is here you have that to amount your life to. Quite sad.<P>You can come with your personal insults all you want. It just proves what a 40 something loser has to offer to this world. I could care less about getting into an argument with you over this game. Because, if all whats happened over these past weeks has shown you anything, it is just a game. You think when I am looking at fighting a war, I could give a ****  who wins a football game on Sunday? It means so little to me now. I will still be passionate about it, but it will never be the same to me. Ever. <P>And FYI, I am going into the Air Force, where they have something called college. It's a place where people go for education (there's one of those big words for you again, and you thought heineken was hard to spell). <P>What you like to insult is what you want the most. <P>p.s. you picked a bad mid-life crisis car, and you got ripped for the installation.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff (AOL IM - FieroTT)<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4 (sold)<BR>Baltimore, MD - MAFOA<BR> <BR>"<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000029||BENGAL4||09-27-2001||06:49 AM||||This post started out to be a fun message regarding a perrenial losing team, beating the world champions. It seems my little friend forgot to keep it in the spirit for which it was intended. Most people like an argument. We can all agree to disagree. His choice in taking this private was not his choice to make, so thats my reason on posting his "PM" message here. <P>As for feeling sorry for me, don't bother. If that is how you picture me, thats fine, but you make alot of assumptions and all that does is make you look like an a$$.<P>I am passionate about the NFL. It is a release from the responsibilities of life, of which you haven't experinenced yet. Try waking up on a Monday morning and your wife, lying beside you, has died of no apparent reason. Then you have to tell 2 little girls that their mother is gone and is never coming back. I wouldn't wish that tradgedy on anyone, but I have become a stronger person because of it.<P>Do I come home from my boring 9 to 5 job, just to get on PFF and argue with people, I think not. You have me beat in the number of posts, 1989 to 397, so who needs a life.<P>If the attack on the WTC has you so upset, why did you reply in the first place? IT IS A DIVERSION. I am devestated and sadden by the events of the last 3 weeks and you are right, our country will never be the same. <P>I applaud you for joining the Air Force. If I was 18, I would be concerned about the looming war. I have a nephew that is in the Marines, my whole family is worried about what is going to happen. Get an education, if the Air Force is the vehicle, great. I was fortunate enough to get my degree from the University of Cincinnati. You won't make any real money without one. So much for insulting what I want. I have it.<P>Finally, as for picking a bad mid-life crisis car, you seemed to like Fieros at one time. What happened? If Fieros are bad, why are you still on this forum? My engine swap has been aggravating to say the least. I am still working the bugs out of it and the problems will be resolved. <P>Am I a 40 year old loser? I think not. Just ask the many friends I have made and cherish from this forum alone. Not bad for a bad mid-life crisis car. <P>Bill<BR>86GT<BR>3800 II S/C<P>||||reg||1
Z||000030||BOILERMAKER||09-27-2001||09:09 AM||||Black88GT<P>All you are doing is showing you are as much of a d**k as most of us already assumed you were as shown in many other posts.  When you start insulting someone that has gone through as much as BENGAL has, you have definitely crossed the line.<P>Don't bother emailing me privately because I'll just post it and show everyone how insignificant you really are.<P>As for ditching the fiero, I'm glad I don't have to relate to a fool like yourself anymore through the cars that we drive.<P>||||reg||8
Z||000031||FieroWife||09-27-2001||12:34 PM||||Black88GT-- What makes you think that you are all that and a bag of chips?  You are going into the Air Force, good for you.  I sincerely applaud you for defending our Country.  However, it does not make you the second coming.  You know nothing about Bill, nothing.  This so called couch potato named Bill comes home from work everyday and then immediately leaves to go coach one of the many sports teams that his daughters participate in.  In spite of  the horrible tragedy he and his family experienced, he rallied to make things right for his girls and those around him.<P>We have all been deeply saddened and terrified by what is occuring in our Country.  ALL OF US, not just you.  People handle things in different ways.  Bill's escape happens to be football.  If your diversion is different, fine.  Just realize that your diversion and the way you handle things makes you no better than anyone else, just different.<P>Scott and I consider ourselves extremely lucky to have a dear friend like Bill, an extremely intelligent, caring and considerate man.  In the future, know what and who you are talking about before YOU run your mouth.||||reg||8
Z||000032||87ECOsomething||09-27-2001||03:04 PM||||I do not see it fair - or my place, for that matter - to personally attack anyone here and I don't fully understand why this turned personal but it has to stop - <B>IMMEDIATELY!!!</B><P>I will, as others have done already, inform you, Jeff, that you will not meet a kinder, gentler, more caring person than Bill!<P>I had the pleasure of meeting him for the first time back in February of 2000 and my life was changed forever!  He has been inspirational, spiritual, motivational, supportive and, without a doubt, the best friend a person could ask for!!!  After seeing him not only survive the many tragedies he's weathered over the past year, but excel as a person - AND A PARENT - through them, I view Bill as something of a gift from God.  A gift that demonstrates, as he has to my family, that you CAN overcome the worst tragedies ... and I consider myself the luckiest man in the world to be able to call him my friend!<P>.<BR>.<BR>.<P>Let's put the boxing gloves away, shake hands, and end this now!||||reg||4
